#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:30
msgid ""
"The orchestra pages are an internal area for members. Accounts are created "
"by the orchestra; there is no self-registration. The pages are hidden from "
"search engines, and the profiles of members cannot be found from outside."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:36
msgid ""
"When you log in, WordPress sets the cookies needed for the login. When you "
"open the link to set a new password, a cookie with your username and the key "
"of the link is set until you have set the password or close the browser. "
"After a form is sent, the browser keeps the scroll position for one minute "
"in its session storage. These are needed for the pages to work; no tracking "
"or analytics takes place."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:44
msgid ""
"Failed logins and requests for a new password do not show whether an account "
"exists. An account receives at most one email with a new password link every "
"few minutes."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:49
msgid ""
"Twice a day, the website asks GitHub (GitHub Inc., USA) whether there are "
"updates of the orchestra plugins. The request contains the address of the "
"website and the versions of WordPress, PHP and the plugins, but no data of "
"members."
msgstr ""

#: src/Ui/EmailMoved.php:39
msgid ""
"Emails are now a plugin of their own: Orchestra Email. Install and activate "
"it to write emails again; your sent emails and emails that are still being "
"sent are kept."
msgstr ""

